sts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:41:03-07:00","id":894287,"title":"","content":"Well, in the pulp-est eras of Mage, Dr Frankenstein himself was an Etherite. He, indeed, created the Monster. But the Monster Awakened (a thing almost unheard off in constructs), and left.<br /> <br /> Mage has &quot;reputation&quot; in the monster creation realm, coupled with some systems (Mind 5 can make it sentient), and characters likely to laugh maniacally while doing it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . You could even create a powerful Talisman that can create the monster if properly used...<br /> <br /> If that fails, well, a Tzimisce with Necromancy may improvize something nasty. Or a Demon with the right Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:56:53-07:00","id":894300,"title":"","content":"In the mage storyteller guide revised there is an actual template to making a &quot;Promethean&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:38:39-07:00","id":894370,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, everyone. Looks like I'll go with Mage for it--Technocracy or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T12:29:50-07:00","id":895631,"title":"","content":"As a GlassWalker player, who's char was a Sociopath metis with weaver like mind And madness<br /> <br /> My plan was to resurrect EVERY fallen garou for the Final Battle a-la Frankenstein...And i happend to stumble with a recently deseased politician. They said it was madness, that It was unethical, but no one thinks about how useful will a sentiant zombie be when fighting the fomor.<br /> <br /> I remember Konietzku saying (read as parody voice) &quot;uhh the comrade is as mad as the wyrm, its an aberration upon gaia&quot; but look who is laughing now with his , zombie army trained to fight the wyrm!<br /> <br /> All it took was to turn the host into a Fetish (not that kind...You pervert), do some espiritual hunting, avoid his soul from reincarnating And Force it back onto his flesh, And voalah. Zombie wolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T13:42:17-07:00","id":895664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/894208-best-way-to-make-something-like-frankenstein-s-monster?p=895631#post895631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a GlassWalker player, who's char was a Sociopath metis with weaver like mind And madness<br /> <br /> My plan was to resurrect EVERY fallen garou for the Final Battle a-la Frankenstein...And i happend to stumble with a recently deseased politician. They said it was madness, that It was unethical, but no one thinks about how useful will a sentiant zombie be when fighting the fomor.<br /> <br /> I remember Konietzku saying (read as parody voice) &quot;uhh the comrade is as mad as the wyrm, its an aberration upon gaia&quot; but look who is laughing now with his , zombie army trained to fight the wyrm!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm, who isn't really affected by physical attempts at assault like that and who gets off on undeath? You basically made the werewolf equivalent of the Black Lantern Corps. More trusted Garou have been killed via Gaia's Vengeful Teeth for less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All it took was to turn the host into a Fetish (not that kind...You pervert), do some espiritual hunting, avoid his soul from reincarnating And Force it back onto his flesh, And voalah. Zombie wolf </div> </div> </div>Reanimator never ends well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:48:00-07:00","id":896525,"title":"","content":"Based on <i>House of Tremere</i> I think the original Gargoyles may be the closest OWoD equivalent. They're stitched together from preserved pieces of dead vampires and then brought back to (un)life in a process not that dissimilar to Frankenstein's Monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:02:06-07:00","id":896566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/894208-best-way-to-make-something-like-frankenstein-s-monster?p=896525#post896525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on <i>House of Tremere</i> I think the original Gargoyles may be the closest OWoD equivalent. They're stitched together from preserved pieces of dead vampires and then brought back to (un)life in a process not that dissimilar to Frankenstein's Monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, they just got stone-skinned vampires with wings, not a whole new thing unto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:45:55-07:00","id":897215,"title":"","content":"That book does have several other varieties of Gargoyles that don't fit the modern horned, bat-winged image. Some of them (particularly the acid-dripping piles of viscera and the flesh-eating insect swarms) are so far removed from humanity I don't know if you could call them vampires anymore. Though they're so masquerade-breaking I'd imagine their creation process hasn't been used in centuries, if the main clan still has people who possess the knowhow at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T00:43:27-07:00","id":897628,"title":"","content":"A Son of the Ether could discover the old Tremere Gargoyle rituals...Surely, he will do a better job than those Hermetics!<br /> Or the secretive and ostracized House of Tremere might ask a Son of the Ether for assistance in regards to improving the Gargoyle creation process.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/894208-best-way-to-make-something-like-frankenstein-s-monster?p=897215#post897215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some of them (particularly the acid-dripping piles of viscera and the flesh-eating insect swarms) are so far removed from humanity I don't know if you could call them vampires anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Skin Eaters aren't one of the strange Gargoyle varieties - they are magical creatures who are ghouled to Gargoyles as part of their creation process.<br /> I always liked the parchment-thin Velluma. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-24-2016, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:17:40-07:00","id":897820,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> <i>Clanbook: Tzimisce</i> Revised has a template called the New Prometheus. The character concept is a compilation of different fleshcrafted bits that survived the Embrace. I recently revisited this template after thinking how diabolically awesome The Creature (<i>Penny Dreadful</i>) would look if he had fangs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Anyhoo, that might be a fun way to explore the whole &quot;What Am I?!?&quot; shtick.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}